"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. The surgical findings included a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) and pathological T2 stage with no extraprostatic extension. Positive surgical margins and absence of seminal vesicle invasion were noted, which are generally favorable. However, the absence of lymph node removal and missing nodal sampling widen the uncertainty regarding regional disease control. The biopsy finding of Acinar adenocarcinoma was consistent with the surgical specimen.\n\nCountervailing factors include the preoperative PSA of 3.8. The lack of documented postoperative PSA or follow-up data significantly limits the ability to assess the trajectory of recurrence. Missing nodal sampling further complicates the assessment of potential nodal involvement. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and their subsequent changes would be crucial in revising this prognosis. The current heuristic horizon suggests a potential recurrence window within the calculated range. The fixed estimated horizon is 42.17 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 27.41–56.92 months; its coverage has not been validated."
